# TalkTally — Technical Architecture

## System Overview
TalkTally consists of a React Native mobile app (Expo) for caregivers and a lightweight Express backend with a PostgreSQL database. The mobile app performs audio calibration and voice detection on-device, stores recordings locally, and uploads session metadata to the server.

## Components
- Mobile App (Expo / React Native)
  - useVoiceDetection hook: calibration, metering, threshold
  - Session screens: prompts, timers, recording management
  - Local persistence: AsyncStorage for deviceId, session queue
- Backend (Express + TypeScript)
  - Routes: POST /sessions, GET /sessions, GET /health
  - Controllers: validate and persist session metadata
  - Database: PostgreSQL (users, sessions)
- Hosting & Infrastructure
  - Backend: Railway (auto SSL), environment variables for DB
  - Database: Railway Postgres

## Data Flow
1. User starts session on mobile → App calibrates microphone
2. On step prompts, app monitors audio, records local audio when child speaks
3. After session complete, app computes accuracy and posts session summary to POST /sessions with deviceId
4. Backend validates and stores metadata in sessions table tied to device_id
5. History screen fetches sessions via GET /sessions?deviceId=...

## Database Schema (summary)
- users (id PK, device_id TEXT UNIQUE, created_at TIMESTAMPTZ)
- sessions (id PK, device_id TEXT FK → users.device_id, accuracy INTEGER, total_steps INTEGER, completed_at TIMESTAMPTZ)
- Index: idx_sessions_device_id ON sessions(device_id)

## Deployment & Environment
- Development: local Postgres, ts-node-dev for backend, Expo dev server for mobile
- Production: Railway for backend and Postgres, Expo builds for mobile releases
- Environment variables required: DATABASE_URL or PGHOST/PGUSER/PGPASSWORD/PGDATABASE/PGPORT, NODE_ENV, PORT

## Monitoring & Observability
- Server logs to console; plan integration with Sentry/Datadog
- Mobile: structured logger utility; plan integration with Sentry for crash reporting

## Security Considerations
- Use parameterized queries (pg) to avoid SQL injection
- Enforce HTTPS for all endpoints; Railway provides managed SSL
- Device ID used as anonymous identifier; do not treat as PII

## Diagram (ASCII)
Mobile (Expo) --HTTPS--> Express API --SQL--> PostgreSQL (Railway)

(See repository docs folder for additional textual diagrams and implementation notes.)
